{
 "answer": "On this Linux host, five named ZIP non-determinism sources plus ZipInfo.create_system each change the sha256 of an asset-only ZIP when left unpinned (two independent packers). Linux-sim vs Windows-sim with the recipe disabled: cde3c2d5f404\u2026 vs 73bb4098d6db\u2026 (differ). Same pair with recipe v1 enabled: both 78e713c6a0f7\u2026 (zipfile) and both stored-packer 9334f985c0bf\u2026. Minimal recipe: ZIP_DEFLATED-9, lexicographic POSIX NFC names, LF text, DOS time 1980-01-01, create_system=3, mode 0o644, empty extra/comment, allowlist text/json/script suffixes, drop .git and __pycache__. Windows side is an in-process behavior simulation (CRLF, backslash, NFD, create_system=0, DOS attrs), not native Win32 zip.exe. SUCCESS:RES-0134 in the receipt AND a two-platform digest pair (Linux-sim vs Windows-sim) plus a both-states control showing the recipe, not an insensitive comparator, causes equality",
